text.section:
The certificate of authority to transact business in the Commonwealth of any foreign corporation may be revoked by order of the Commission when it finds that such foreign corporation:

Has continued to exceed the authority conferred upon it by law;


Has failed to maintain a registered office or a registered agent in the Commonwealth as required by law;


Has failed to file any document required by this chapter to be filed with the Commission;


No longer exists under the laws of the jurisdiction of its formation; or


Has been convicted for a violation of 8 U.S.C. § 1324a(f), as amended, for actions of its officers and directors constituting a pattern or practice of employing unauthorized aliens in the Commonwealth.
				A certificate of authority revoked pursuant to subdivision A 5 shall not be eligible for reinstatement for a period of not less than one year.
